# Modbus Protocol and Register Handling

## Protocol Overview
The LXP Bridge communicates with EG4 18kpv inverters using Modbus RTU over TCP. Reference the official protocol: [EG4-18KPV-12LV-Modbus-Protocol.pdf](https://www.dth.net/solar/luxpower/modbus/EG4-18KPV-12LV-Modbus-Protocol.pdf)

## Register Categories

### Input Registers (Read-Only)
- **System Status** (Register 0): Operating mode and state information
- **PV System** (Registers 1-19): Solar panel voltages, power, and battery status
- **Grid Connection** (Registers 20-39): Grid voltage, frequency, and power data
- **EPS System** (Registers 40-59): Emergency power supply status
- **Energy Counters** (Registers 60-99): Daily and total energy production
- **Fault Codes** (Registers 140-159): System faults and warnings
- **Temperature** (Registers 160-179): Component temperature monitoring
- **Battery Management** (Registers 180-199): Battery status and BMS information

### Holding Registers (Read/Write)
- **System Configuration** (Registers 0-19): Model, serial, firmware, time settings
- **PV Configuration** (Registers 20-39): PV input mode and thresholds
- **Grid Protection** (Registers 25-40): Voltage and frequency limits
- **Power Control** (Registers 64-83): Charge/discharge rates and SOC limits
- **Advanced Features** (Registers 181-250): Volt-Watt, Volt-Var, TOU settings

## Critical Bitmasks

### Register 21 - Function Enable/Disable
- **Bit 0**: EPS Enable (Emergency Power Supply)
- **Bit 1**: Over Frequency Load Derate Enable
- **Bit 2**: DRMS Enable (Demand Response Management)
- **Bit 3**: Low Voltage Ride Through Enable
- **Bit 4**: Anti-Islanding Enable
- **Bit 5**: Neutral Detection Enable
- **Bit 6**: Grid On Power Soft Start Enable
- **Bit 7**: AC Charge Enable
- **Bit 8**: Switch Seamless Enable
- **Bit 9**: Set to Standby Enable
- **Bit 10**: Forced Discharge Enable
- **Bit 11**: Charge Priority Enable
- **Bit 12**: ISO Enable
- **Bit 13**: GFCI Enable (Ground Fault Circuit Interrupter)
- **Bit 14**: DCI Enable (DC Isolation)
- **Bit 15**: Feed In Grid Enable

### Register 110 - Advanced Functions
- **Bit 0**: PV Off Grid Enable
- **Bit 1**: Fast Zero Export Enable
- **Bit 2**: Micro Grid Enable
- **Bit 3**: Shared Battery Enable
- **Bit 4**: Charge Last Enable

## Data Validation Rules

### Voltage Ranges
- **PV Voltage**: 0-1000V (0.1V resolution)
- **Battery Voltage**: 0-100V (0.1V resolution)
- **Grid Voltage**: 0-300V (0.1V resolution)
- **EPS Voltage**: 0-300V (0.1V resolution)

### Frequency Ranges
- **Grid Frequency**: 45-65Hz (0.01Hz resolution)
- **EPS Frequency**: 45-65Hz (0.01Hz resolution)

### Power and Energy
- **Inverter Power**: 0-18000W (1W resolution)
- **Energy Values**: Always positive, cumulative (0.1kWh resolution)

## Implementation Guidelines

### Register Access
- Use proper register addressing (0-based indexing)
- Handle multi-word registers with little-endian byte order
- Implement proper error handling for communication failures
- Validate register values against expected ranges

### Bit Manipulation
- When modifying bitmasks, read current value, modify specific bits, write back
- Use bitwise operations for setting/clearing individual flags
- Preserve existing bit values when making changes

### Error Handling
- Monitor fault codes (Registers 140-141) for system issues
- Check warning codes (Registers 142-143) for potential problems
- Implement proper timeout and retry logic for Modbus operations
- Log all register read/write operations for debugging
